        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/gui/server.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "refactor",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:17:04Z",
          "note": "gui/server.ts: The RouteHandler type alias (type RouteHandler = () => Promise<unknown>) was removed as part of this WP since it was only used by matchRoute(). No external consumers were found."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:17:04Z",
          "note": "gui/docs/agents/project-manifest/api-surface.md, data-flows.md, constraints.md: These agent-context doc files still reference matchRoute() in their descriptions (e.g. 'GET routes are handled by matchRoute()'). These are out of scope for this WP but should be updated in the Documentation phase to reflect the unified dispatchRoute() pattern."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:17:04Z",
          "note": "gui/server.ts buildRoutes(): The routes object array is now approximately 450 lines. A future improvement would be to split the route table into logical sub-builders (e.g. buildProjectRoutes, buildKnowledgeRoutes) and compose them in buildRoutes(). This would improve readability without changing behaviour. Not implemented as it is out of scope for this WP."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:17:04Z",
          "note": "gui/server.ts dispatchRoute(): The dispatchRoute() function rebuilds the full route table on every request via buildRoutes(). For high-frequency endpoints, caching the compiled route table (e.g. memoizing by ledgerRoot+configPath) would avoid repeated array allocations. Low impact at current traffic levels."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-23T16:17:30Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-23T16:21:02Z",
      "duration_ms": 212000,
      "summary": [
        "Verified all 7 acceptance criteria via code inspection, static analysis, and test execution. AC1: matchRoute() absent from server.ts (grep confirmed zero matches). AC2: handleRequest() has exactly one dispatchRoute() call — single dispatch path, no secondary routing. AC3: JSDoc comment block on buildRoutes() explicitly states Section B MUST precede Section C as load-bearing (not cosmetic), with concrete explanation of the shadowing risk. AC4: Static analysis confirmed 52 parameterised regex path entries with 83 named capture groups and 0 positional capture groups. AC5: All targeted tests pass — 77 tests across gui-server.test.ts, route-structured-format.test.ts, server-body-limit.test.ts, server-error-mapping.test.ts, server-info.test.ts, server-knowledge-routes.test.ts, server-queue.test.ts, security-headers.test.ts. Full GUI regression also passes: 55 test files, 1624 tests. AC6: Section B/C ordering verified — deprecated /:slug/keyword routes match correctly before Section C catch-alls. /api/projects/my-project/plan, /synthesis, /health, /work-packages, /work-packages/overview, /work-packages/:wpId, /dialogues, /runs all resolve via Section B routes. AC7: parseQueryString() integration confirmed — all query-parameter routes (GET /api/projects, /api/knowledge, /api/repos, /:repo/:slug/dialogues, /:repo/:slug/chunks, /:repo/:slug/runs/:filename?after=N) forward query args correctly. Percent-encoded values decode transparently. Bare ? returns empty URLSearchParams safely."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "55 test files (gui suite) + 8 targeted server test files",
        "tests_passed": 1701,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:21:02Z",
          "note": "Edge case: GET /api/projects/:repo/:slug/runs/:filename?after=-1 passes -1 as a valid integer to the handler. The server-side code does not reject negative `after` values — this is acceptable as handler-level validation responsibility, not a routing defect."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:21:02Z",
          "note": "The deprecated GET /:slug/runs route resolves via resolveProjectDir() and falls back to the legacy flat path. This is correct, but its test coverage is through integration paths rather than a dedicated test. No regression observed, but a targeted unit test would harden this."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-07-23T16:09:21Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-07-23T16:21:02Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:17:04Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 50+ routes are now in buildRoutes() with the Section A/B/C organization. The old matchRoute() is fully deleted. handleRequest() is now a clean ~35-line function. The RouteHandler type alias was also removed as it was only used by matchRoute(). parseQueryString() is retained (used by dispatchRoute() internally). The 52 named capture groups span all parameterised routes — verified by grep. QA should focus on: (1) deprecated keyword-specific routes (/:slug/plan, /:slug/synthesis, etc.) resolving correctly via Section B before Section C catch-alls, (2) query-parameter routes (GET /api/projects, GET /api/knowledge, GET /api/repos, GET /api/projects/:slug/dialogues, GET /api/projects/:slug/chunks, GET /api/projects/:slug/runs/:filename?after=N) forwarding query args correctly through the dispatcher."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:21:02Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 7 ACs verified PASS. 1701 tests pass across 63 test files with zero failures. Key areas confirmed: matchRoute() fully removed, single dispatchRoute() call in handleRequest(), 52 regex routes all using named capture groups (0 positional), Section B deprecated keyword routes correctly shadow Section C catch-alls, and all query-parameter routes correctly receive args via dispatcher's query argument. Code is clean and ready for code review."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

